codex
One audit correction: the first operation count treated a modular inverse as one step. Counting square-and-multiply inversions makes the compact route about 70 field operations per panel, so ten panels would violate G9(c). I’m shrinking only the batch count—not the degree haystack—to four hard panels. That keeps the witness fixed at 16 atoms, preserves roughly a million mechanical operations, and restores an honest ≤300-operation route.
