codex
Built a self-contained Track B generator for affine isomorphisms of split homogeneous binary forms over finite fields. This follows the paper’s Polynomial Isomorphism Search Problem in Section 8; Section 10’s efficient-solvability discussion rules out an honest Track A claim. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2511.06843)

Local results:

- G1–G8 pass, including 0/200,000 random guesses.
- Reference algorithm: 1,427,306 field operations, 0.028524 seconds.
- Compact invariant route: at most 280 exact operations.
- Answer: 86 characters and 16 atoms.
- Canonicalization passed relabelling, non-collapse, and diversity tests.
- Final G1 recheck: 12/12.

The result is parked, not shipped or rejected: all bare, structural-hint, and placebo oracle calls returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” leaving G9 and STEP 4 unmeasured.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.06843/gen_2511_06843.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.06843/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.06843/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.06843/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.06843/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.06843/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)
- [Parking record](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.06843/PARKED.md)

Restoring OpenRouter quota and rerunning the three harness arms is the only remaining requirement.
